.TH AVR\-RUN\-LOGS 1 "" "avr 0.2.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-run-logs \- Fetch logs for a workflow run's GitHub jobs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr run logs
[OPTIONS] RUN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetch logs for a workflow run's GitHub jobs.
.PP
RUN accepts the same Avrea IDs, GitHub run IDs, and run URLs as `avr run view`.
.PP
Long-form alternative to `avr run view --log[-failed]`. Use --follow to tail logs in real time for an in-progress job; pass --job to scope to a specific job when a run has many.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr run logs run-abc123
    avr run logs run-abc123 --failed
    avr run logs run-abc123 --job test
    avr run logs run-abc123 --follow
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIRUN\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug.
.TP
\fB\-\-job\fR \fITEXT\fR
Restrict to GitHub jobs whose name contains this string.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-follow\fR
Tail logs as they appear (running jobs only).
.TP
\fB\-\-failed\fR
Show only logs from failed jobs.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-levels\fR
Include diagnostic-level lines (off by default).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print directly to stdout instead of paging through `less`. Same as setting AVR_PAGER=''.
.SH SEE ALSO
